00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.140
Film Courage: What is a scene?

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:06.000
Jen Grisanti, Speaker/Story/Career Consultant,&nbsp;
Author: A scene is like one step toward the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.940
bigger picture. In the scene you're looking at&nbsp;
who wants what and what is getting in the way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:22.260
Who wants what, what is getting in the way, how&nbsp;
do you create the small piece of the bigger puzzle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:32.580
through looking at the scene and also&nbsp;
understanding what is the conflict in the scene is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:41.100
a struggle that I see a lot of writers go through.&nbsp;
You often will find scenes that have no conflict&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:50.820
and you have no sense of who wants what and what&nbsp;
is getting in the way. By simply understanding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.820 --> 00:01:00.000
the scene as a part of the greater picture and&nbsp;
how you are creating a step toward an outcome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:05.940
while escalating the conflict is&nbsp;
an important part of scene work.

